{"name":"Sun God","hex":"#dfba5a","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sun god","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A personification of the sun worshipped as a god."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sun_god"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sun God (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Sun God is the debut studio album by Sun God, released on May 22, 1995, by Fifth Colvmn Records and Original Artists Group."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c0/Sun_God_-_Sun_God.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sun_God_(album)","wikidata":"Q104854956"},{"title":"Sun God (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Sun God were a European electronic music group comprising musicians Rodney Orpheus, Marcus Giltjes, and Patricia Nigiani. The band released one studio album titled Sun God in 1995 for Fifth Colvmn Records and Original Artists Group."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sun_God_(band)","wikidata":"Q104854954"},{"title":"Solar deity","blocks":[{"text":"A solar deity or sun deity is a deity who represents the Sun or an aspect thereof. Such deities are usually associated with power and strength. Solar deities and Sun worship can be found throughout most of recorded history in various forms. The English word sun derives from Proto-Germanic *sunnǭ. The Sun is sometimes referred to by its Latin name Sol or by its Greek name Helios."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Ilion---metopa.jpg/330px-Ilion---metopa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solar_deity","wikidata":"Q511056"},{"title":"Sun","blocks":[{"text":"The Sun is the star located at the centre of the Solar System. It is a massive sphere of hot plasma, heated to incandescence by nuclear fusion reactions in its core, radiating the energy from its surface mainly as visible light and infrared radiation, 